    N_('The Areopagus, or Mars Hill: the rocky height below the Athenian Acropolis where the city\'s council met. Acts sets here Paul\'s address to the philosophers, taking their altar \'to an unknown god\' as his starting point for the God who \'made the world and everything in it.\''),
