    N_('The Great Theatre of Ephesus'),
    N_('Ephesus'),
    N_('Excavated by the Austrian Archaeological Institute, from 1895'),
    N_('The great theatre of Ephesus, which held some 25,000 people. Acts sets here the riot of the silversmiths, who feared Paul\'s preaching would ruin the trade in silver shrines of Artemis and filled the theatre with the chant, \'Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!\''),
