    N_('rebuilt after 356 BC'),
    N_('Site located by John Turtle Wood, 1869'),
    N_('A single re-erected column marks the temple of Artemis at Ephesus, once counted among the seven wonders of the world. The cult of \'Artemis of the Ephesians,\' and the craftsmen who profited from it, form the backdrop to the uproar Paul\'s preaching stirred in the city.'),
    N_('The Erastus Inscription'),
    N_('Excavated in situ at Corinth'),
    N_('A paving stone by the theatre of Corinth, its bronze letters lost but their cut sockets still legible: \'Erastus, in return for his aedileship, laid this at his own expense.\' Many identify this magistrate with the Erastus, \'the city treasurer,\' whom Paul names sending greetings from Corinth, though the identification is not certain.'),
