    N_('Excavated by Yohanan Aharoni, 1962–67'),
    N_('The desert fortress of Arad, holding one of the very few Israelite temples yet excavated: a courtyard with a sacrificial altar and a small inner shrine, apparently taken out of use during a religious reform of the kind the Bible credits to Hezekiah, who \'removed the high places\' to centre worship on Jerusalem.'),
    N_('The Herodian Temple Stones'),
    N_('1st century BC'),
    N_('Standing site, Jerusalem'),
    N_('The massive Herodian ashlars of the Western Wall, part of the retaining wall Herod the Great raised to enlarge the Temple platform. These are the kind of stones behind a disciple\'s awe, \'what wonderful stones and what wonderful buildings,\' and Jesus\' reply that not one would be left upon another.'),
    N_('The Synagogue at Capernaum'),
