    N_('The white limestone synagogue of Capernaum, the lakeside town that was the base of Jesus\' Galilean ministry. This building is later (4th–5th century), but it rests on the black basalt foundations of the 1st-century synagogue where, the Gospels say, Jesus taught and healed.'),
    N_('A Judean Pillar Figurine'),
    N_('Judah'),
    N_('Excavated; common in Judahite homes'),
    N_('Small clay figurines of a woman supporting her breasts, mass-produced and found by the hundreds in ordinary Judahite houses. Their exact meaning is debated (fertility, protection, a goddess), but they put a face on the popular household religion the prophets kept condemning, when even in Jerusalem families baked cakes for \'the queen of heaven.\''),
